IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art75d: Article 75d, safeguards and further specification (inserted by the Omnibus, `▼M1 INSERTED`). LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). Only the amended text exists: the Article is new.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 75d act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 75d(2) respect fully the rights of defence and of access to the file of the operator`
    `Art 75d(2) adopt a decision setting out the terms of disclosure`
    `Art 75d(2) obtain access to confidential information or internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States`
    `Art 75d(3) adopt implementing acts concerning the practical arrangements for access to the file and the negotiated disclosure of information`
    `Art 75d(4) publish the decisions adopted pursuant to Articles 75b and 75c`

-- src:1254 | 1. Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis to operators subject to the AI Office’s competence pursuant to Article 75(1) of this Regulation, without prejudice to more specific procedural rights provided for in this Regulation.
@ref Art 75d(1) (src:1254)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator is subject to the AI Office's competence pursuant to Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(1) Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 applies mutatis mutandis to the operator` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the operator is subject to the AI Office's competence pursuant to Article 75(1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "operators subject to the AI Office's competence pursuant to Article 75(1)", with no "only" (ruling (c)); "without prejudice to more specific procedural rights provided for in this Regulation" does not change the answer

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) first sentence (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator falls within the scope of Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(2) first sentence the rights of defence and of access to the file of the operator are fully respected in proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the operator falls within the scope of Article 75(1)` AND `the matter is in proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1)" "in proceedings", with no "only"

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) first sentence (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator falls within the scope of Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75d act`
`Art 75d(2) first sentence the AI Office's duty to respect the rights of defence and of access to the file` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the operator falls within the scope of Article 75(1)`) OR (NOT `the matter is in proceedings`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 75d(2) respect fully the rights of defence and of access to the file of the operator`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) second sentence (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator falls within the scope of Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a decision on the basis of Article 75c(1) may be adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(2) second sentence the operator is entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the operator falls within the scope of Article 75(1)` AND `a decision on the basis of Article 75c(1) may be adopted`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is for "those operators" "in view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1)", and "subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets" (an "entitled" function: listed with a count in NOTES.md, not decided)

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) third sentence (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the parties disagree on the terms of disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(2) third sentence the AI Office may adopt decisions setting out the terms of disclosure` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the parties disagree on the terms of disclosure`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties" (a power gated by "in the case of": split site (ii), fork F-75d-2-disagreement)

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) third sentence (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the parties disagree on the terms of disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75d act`
`Art 75d(2) third sentence the AI Office's choice to adopt decisions setting out the terms of disclosure` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the parties disagree on the terms of disclosure`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MAY `Art 75d(2) adopt a decision setting out the terms of disclosure`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) fourth and fifth sentences (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the material is confidential information or an internal document of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States, or correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(2) fourth and fifth sentences the right of access to the file is barred from extending to the material` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the material is confidential information or an internal document of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States, or correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities" (a flat negative: the bar holds)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is about this material and nothing else

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) fourth and fifth sentences (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator seeks access to the AI Office file` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75d act`
`Art 75d(2) the operator's bar on obtaining access to the confidential information and internal documents` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the operator seeks access to the AI Office file`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is barred: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the bar is about do not all hold
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party operator`
        SHANT `Art 75d(2) obtain access to confidential information or internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party operator` BECAUSE "the operator obtained access to confidential information or internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States"

-- src:1255 | 2. The rights of defence and of access to the file of operators falling within the scope of Article 75(1) shall be fully respected in proceedings. In view of the possible adoption of decisions on the basis of Article 75c(1), those operators shall be entitled to have access to the AI Office file under the terms of a negotiated disclosure, subject to the legitimate interest of the operator or other person concerned in the protection of their business secrets. The AI Office shall have the power to adopt decisions setting out such terms of disclosure in the case of disagreement between the parties. The right of access to the file shall not extend to confidential information and internal documents of the AI Office, the Board, competent market surveillance authorities or other public authorities of the Member States. In particular, the right of access shall not extend to correspondence between the AI Office and those authorities. Nothing in this paragraph shall prevent the AI Office from disclosing and using information necessary to prove an infringement.
@ref Art 75d(2) sixth sentence (src:1255)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information is necessary to prove an infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(2) sixth sentence nothing in the paragraph prevents the AI Office from disclosing and using the information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the information is necessary to prove an infringement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "information necessary to prove an infringement"

-- src:1256 | 3. The Commission may adopt implementing acts concerning the practical arrangements for access to the file and the negotiated disclosure of information provided for in paragraph 2.
@ref Art 75d(3) (src:1256)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(3) the Commission may adopt implementing acts concerning the practical arrangements for access to the file and the negotiated disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "The Commission may adopt implementing acts concerning the practical arrangements for access to the file and the negotiated disclosure of information provided for in paragraph 2"

-- src:1256 | 3. The Commission may adopt implementing acts concerning the practical arrangements for access to the file and the negotiated disclosure of information provided for in paragraph 2.
@ref Art 75d(3) (src:1256)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75d act`
`Art 75d(3) the Commission's choice to adopt implementing acts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party Commission`
        MAY `Art 75d(3) adopt implementing acts concerning the practical arrangements for access to the file and the negotiated disclosure of information`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1257 | 4. The AI Office shall publish the decisions it adopts pursuant to Articles 75b and 75c. Such publication shall state the names of the parties and the main content of the decision, including any penalties imposed. The publication shall have regard to the rights and legitimate interests of any person concerned in the protection of their confidential information.
@ref Art 75d(4) first sentence (src:1257)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the decision is adopted pursuant to Article 75b or 75c` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75d(4) first sentence the AI Office must publish the decisions it adopts pursuant to Articles 75b and 75c` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the decision is adopted pursuant to Article 75b or 75c`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the decisions it adopts pursuant to Articles 75b and 75c", with no "only"

-- src:1257 | 4. The AI Office shall publish the decisions it adopts pursuant to Articles 75b and 75c. Such publication shall state the names of the parties and the main content of the decision, including any penalties imposed. The publication shall have regard to the rights and legitimate interests of any person concerned in the protection of their confidential information.
